3. Recommend Approach:

Maintain a dedicated heartbeat table:

CREATE TABLE replication_heartbeat (id int primary key,ts timestamptz);

Publisher updates every few seconds:

UPDATE replication_heartbeat SET ts = clock_timestamp() WHERE id = 1;

Subscriber measures:
SELECT clock_timestamp() - ts AS replication_delay FROM replication_heartbeat WHERE id = 1;

This provides the actual end-to-end latency experienced by applications:

Commit on publisher
    ↓
WAL generation
    ↓
Logical decoding
    ↓
Network transfer
    ↓
Apply worker
    ↓
Visible on subscriber

Unlike LSN lag, a heartbeat directly measures what users care about: "How old is the data on the subscriber?"


